  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.10966v1</id>
    <title>MMTB: Evaluating Terminal Agents on Multimedia-File Tasks</title>
    <updated>2026-05-08T10:57:19Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.10966v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.10966v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Terminals provide a powerful interface for AI agents by exposing diverse tools for automating complex workflows, yet existing terminal-agent benchmarks largely focus on tasks grounded in text, code, and structured files. However, many real-world workflows require practitioners to work directly with audio and video files. Working with such multimedia files calls for terminal agents not only to understand multimedia content, but also to convert auditory and visual evidence across related files into appropriate actions. To evaluate terminal agents on multimedia-file tasks, we introduce MultiMedia-TerminalBench (MMTB), a benchmark of 105 tasks across 5 meta-categories where terminal agents directly operate with audio and video files. Alongside MMTB, we propose Terminus-MM, a multimedia harness that extends Terminus-KIRA with audio and video perception for terminal agents. Together, MMTB and Terminus-MM support a controlled study of multimedia terminal agents, revealing how different forms of multimedia access shape task outcomes and determine which evidence agents rely on to construct executable terminal workflows. MMTB media and metadata are released at https://huggingface.co/datasets/mm-tbench/mmtb-media</summary>
    <category term="cs.MM" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-05-08T10:57:19Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.MM"/>
